---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeExample from '../../components/CodeExample.astro';
const files: [string, string][] = [
  ['index.json', 'What this release contains: schema and dataset versions, counts, the endpoint templates below, and links to the usage terms.'],
  ['registry.json', 'The whole database in one file: sets, cards, printings and the three histories.'],
  ['registry.json.sha256', 'Its SHA-256, in sha256sum format.'],
  ['schema.json', 'The JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) the whole database validates against.'],
  ['changes.json', 'What this release changed against the previous one: counts, the ids behind them, and identifiers_removed, always 0 within a major. From v3.3.2 on.'],
  ['types.d.ts', 'TypeScript declarations generated from schema.json: import type { Registry, Card } from "./types". From v3.3.3 on.'],
  ['cards/{codex_id}.json', 'One card, plus summaries of its printings, its name history and its card history.'],
  ['printings/{printing_id}.json', 'One printing, plus its slug history.'],
  ['slugs/{slug}.json', 'Resolves any slug, current or old, to its permanent IDs.'],
  ['sets.json', 'The set catalogue: one entry per set with counts.'],
  ['sets/{set_code}.json', 'One set, plus the list of its cards and their printing IDs.'],
  ['index/cards.json', 'Compact card records for search and filtering.'],
  ['index/printings.json', 'Compact printing records, with image_hash and image_status.'],
  ['index/slugs.json', 'An object mapping every slug ever issued to its printing_id.'],
  ['history/cards.json', 'Every recorded gameplay face of every card.'],
  ['history/names.json', 'Every recorded card name and when it was in force.'],
  ['history/slugs.json', 'Every recorded slug and when it was in force.'],
];
const curl = `curl --fail --location \\
  --user-agent 'my-card-tool/1.0 (contact@example.com)' \\
  'https://api.kairosarchive.net/v3/slugs/004-witch-b-s.json'`;
---
<Docs title="Endpoints" description="Every endpoint is a file under a release folder. Same names under every release.">
  <p>All paths below are relative to a release root (<code>/v3.3.0/</code>) or the <code>/v3/</code> alias. They are static files with no query parameters. To search, <a href="/docs/data">download the data</a> or an index and filter locally, or use the <a href="/docs/query">query API</a>, <code>/cards?q=…</code>, which runs the site's search syntax on the API domain.</p>

  <h2>The files</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>What you get</th></tr></thead><tbody>{files.map(([path, what]) => <tr><td><code class="endpoint">{path}</code></td><td>{what}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>

  <h2>What a per-object file adds</h2>
  <p>A record in <code>registry.json</code> and the same record's own file carry the same fields. The file adds what you would otherwise have to join yourself:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A card file</strong> adds <code>printings</code> (a summary of each printing: id, slug, set, release date, product, finish, whether it shows the current values, retirement date), <code>name_history</code> and <code>card_history</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>A printing file</strong> adds <code>slug_history</code>: every slug that printing has ever had.</li>
    <li><strong>A slug file</strong> is a small resolver: the slug, its <code>printing_id</code> and <code>codex_id</code>, the card's name, the printing's current slug and whether the one you asked for is current, the dates the slug was in force, set, product, finish, retirement date, and links.</li>
    <li><strong>A set file</strong> replaces the catalogue's <code>cards</code> count with a <code>cards</code> array: each card's id and name and its printing IDs in that set, ordered by name (the official data has no collector numbers).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What the indexes contain</h2>
  <p>The indexes are for building a search box without loading 6 MB. They hold selected fields, not full records, and no links.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>index/cards.json</code>: id, name, type, category, rarity, elements, keywords, subtypes, cost, attack, defense, power, life, errata, set codes, default printing and image status.</li>
    <li><code>index/printings.json</code>: printing id, card id, slug, set code, product, finish, whether it shows the current values, retirement date, <code>image_hash</code> and <code>image_status</code>. With the hash you can <a href="/docs/images">build any image address</a> without fetching the printing.</li>
    <li><code>index/slugs.json</code>: one object, slug to <code>printing_id</code>, for every slug ever issued.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Make a request</h2>
  <CodeExample code={curl} lang="bash" title="curl · resolve a slug through the alias" />
  <p>Check the status before parsing. A slug that was never issued returns <code>404</code>; a retired printing still resolves. <a href="/docs/errors">Errors</a> lists every status.</p>
</Docs>
